g Valley (adventure, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Hadimba Devi Temple (temple, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Mall Road (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: evening)\n  - Beas River Rafting (adventure, ₹600 entry, best: morning)\n  - Old Manali (culture, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Vashisht Hot Springs (wellness, ₹50 entry, best: morning)\n\nResearch Brief:\nHey there, fellow traveler! Get ready for an amazing 5-day adventure in Manali. Our research team has pulled together a concise brief to help you make the most of your budget-friendly trip.\n\n### 1. Weather & What to Pack\n\nYour trip falls during a period with pleasant daytime temperatures, ranging from **29.4°C to 30.8°C**. This means light cotton clothing will be perfect for exploring during the day. However, Manali's mountain weather is known for its surprises:\n*   **Evening Chill:** Temperatures drop sharply after sunset, even in summer. **Always carry a jacket or a light woollen sweater** for evenings.\n*   **Rain Ready:** The advisory suggests carrying **rain gear and waterproof covers for your bags**. Mountain weather can be unpredictable, with sudden showers possible.\n*   **Best Time \n\nRecommended Hotel: Backpacker's Inn Manali (₹650/night, rating: 3.8)\nRecommended Transport: bus (₹650, 14 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹1,300, Hotel ₹2,600, Food ₹2,175, Activities ₹750"}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'max_tokens': 8192, 'temperature': 0.7}}
