i, 3 days\nBudget: ₹15,000 for 1 traveler(s)\nStyle: budget\n\nWeather: Day 1: 5-15C, Day 2: 6-16C, Day 3: 7-17C\nAdvisory: [Mock data] Cool weather — carry light jackets and layered clothing; carry rain gear and waterproof covers for bags; temperatures drop sharply after sunset even in summer — always carry a jacket.\n\nTop Places:\n  - Rohtang Pass (scenic, ₹550 entry, best: morning)\n  - Solang Valley (adventure, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Hadimba Devi Temple (temple, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Mall Road (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: evening)\n  - Beas River Rafting (adventure, ₹600 entry, best: morning)\n  - Old Manali (culture, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Vashisht Hot Springs (wellness, ₹50 entry, best: morning)\n\nResearch Brief:\nHello Traveler! Get ready for an amazing 3-day budget adventure in the beautiful mountains of Manali. Here’s your concise research brief to help you make the most of your trip:\n\n---\n\n### PariKrama Research Brief: Manali (3 Days, Budget)\n\n**1. Weather Summary & What to Pack:**\n*   **Temperatures:** Expect cool weather with daytime temperatures ranging from 5-17°C. Evenings will be significantly chillier.\n*   **Packing Essentials:** Layering is key! Pack light jackets or sweaters for the day, and a warmer jacket for evenings. **Rain gear (waterproof jacket, bag cover)** is a must, as mountain weather can be unpredictable. Comfortable walking shoes are essential for exploring.\n*   **Best Time for Activities:** Most outdoor activities are best enjoyed during the day when temperatures are milde\n\nHotel Options (choose the best fit for each night):\n  - Himalayan Hideaway Hostel (hostel, ₹780/night, rating: 4.1, location: Old Manali)\n  - Beas Valley Inn (budget_hotel, ₹1,950/night, rating: 3.7, location: Near Mall Road)\nRecommended Transport: bus (₹650, 14 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹1,300, Hotel ₹1,560, Food ₹1,620, Activities ₹400'}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'max_tokens': 8192, 'temperature': 0.7}}
