i, 5 days\nBudget: ₹15,000 for 2 traveler(s)\nStyle: budget\n\nWeather: Day 1: 30.8-30.9C, Day 2: 30.0-30.0C, Day 3: 29.4-29.4C, Day 4: 28.4-28.4C, Day 5: 30.0-30.0C\nAdvisory: Pleasant temperatures — light cotton clothing is fine; carry rain gear and waterproof covers for bags; temperatures drop sharply after sunset even in summer — always carry a jacket.\n\nTop Places:\n  - Rohtang Pass (scenic, ₹550 entry, best: morning)\n  - Solang Valley (adventure, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Hadimba Devi Temple (temple, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Mall Road (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: evening)\n  - Beas River Rafting (adventure, ₹600 entry, best: morning)\n  - Old Manali (culture, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Vashisht Hot Springs (wellness, ₹50 entry, best: morning)\n\nResearch Brief:\nHey there, fellow traveler! Get ready for an awesome 5-day budget adventure in Manali. Here's your quick research brief to make the most of your trip:\n\n---\n\n### **PariKrama Research Brief: Manali - 5-Day Budget Trip**\n\n**1. Weather & What to Pack**\nExpect pleasant, warm days with temperatures hovering around **29-31°C**. This is perfect for exploring! However, the advisory is spot on: temperatures can drop significantly after sunset, even in summer.\n*   **Pack:** Light cotton clothing for the day. **Crucially, carry a light jacket or fleece for evenings.**\n*   **Rain Gear:** The advisory also mentions carrying rain gear and waterproof covers for bags. This hints at potential sudden showers, so be prepared!\n*   **Best Time for Activities:** These temperatures are ideal for outdoor adventure\n\nHotel Options (choose the best fit for each night):\n  - Backpacker's Den Manali (hostel, ₹650/night, rating: 4.1, location: Old Town Area, Manali)\n  - Hotel Valley View Manali (budget_hotel, ₹1,560/night, rating: 3.9, location: Main Road, Manali)\nRecommended Transport: bus (₹650, 14 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹2,600, Hotel ₹2,600, Food ₹5,700, Activities ₹600"}], 'model': 'llama