i, 7 days\nBudget: ₹15,000 for 1 traveler(s)\nStyle: budget\n\nWeather: Day 1: 36.0-37.2C, Day 2: 29.2-29.2C, Day 3: 29.4-29.4C, Day 4: 29.5-29.5C, Day 5: 29.9-29.9C\nAdvisory: Pleasant temperatures — light cotton clothing is fine; temperatures drop sharply after sunset even in summer — always carry a jacket.\n\nTop Places:\n  - Rohtang Pass (scenic, ₹550 entry, best: morning)\n  - Solang Valley (adventure, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Hadimba Devi Temple (temple, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Mall Road (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: evening)\n  - Beas River Rafting (adventure, ₹600 entry, best: morning)\n  - Old Manali (culture, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Vashisht Hot Springs (wellness, ₹50 entry, best: morning)\n\nResearch Brief:\nHey there, PariKrama adventurer! Get ready for an amazing 7-day budget trip to Manali. Here’s your concise and actionable research brief to make the most of your adventure:\n\n---\n\n### Manali Budget Brief: 7 Days of Himalayan Bliss\n\n**1. Weather & What to Pack**\nYour trip falls during a period of **pleasant day temperatures**, ranging from **29-37°C**. This means **light cotton clothing** will be perfect for exploring during the day. However, Manali's mountain climate means temperatures drop *sharply* after sunset, even in summer. **Always carry a jacket, fleece, or light woollens** for comfortable evenings.\n*   **Best time for activities:** Mornings and late afternoons are ideal for sightseeing and adventure sports when the sun isn't at its peak.\n*   **Monsoon Watch (June-September):** Whil\n\nHotel Options (choose the best fit for each night):\n  - Backpacker's Den Manali (hostel, ₹650/night, rating: 4.1, location: Old Town Area, Manali)\n  - Hotel Valley View Manali (budget_hotel, ₹1,560/night, rating: 3.9, location: Main Road, Manali)\nRecommended Transport: bus (₹650, 14 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹1,300, Hotel ₹3,900, Food ₹3,940, Activities ₹1,200"}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'max_tokens': 8192, 'tempe